MASTER EXECUTIVE DIRECTIVE

Build LINGUAVERSE AI as a premium, intelligent, voice-first language-learning and real-world communication training platform.

LINGUAVERSE AI is not another vocabulary memorization application, grammar quiz platform, or generic AI chatbot.

It must connect five essential activities:

1. Learning a language.
2. Practicing communication.
3. Detecting actual mistakes.
4. Correcting weaknesses.
5. Measuring whether the learner improves.

The platform must create a continuous, personalized, explainable and evidence-based learning experience.

0.1 Non-negotiable principles

- Never claim functionality that has not been implemented and tested.
- Never generate fake user activity, learning progress, revenue, reviews, testimonials, approvals or analytics.
- Never present AI-generated guesses as verified educational assessments.
- Never award proficiency levels without sufficient assessment evidence.
- Never claim pronunciation accuracy without appropriate acoustic evidence.
- Never expose API keys, credentials or provider secrets in frontend code.
- Never bypass backend authorization.
- Never use private voice recordings for model training without appropriate consent and legal basis.
- Never overwrite an existing repository without auditing it.
- Never create duplicate components, tables, services or API routes unnecessarily.
- Never delete production data through routine migrations.
- Every important operation must have a verifiable backend implementation.
- Every AI evaluation must be testable, explainable and traceable.
- Every sensitive administrative operation must be audited.
- Every implementation phase must produce evidence-based completion reports.
- Accessibility, privacy, reliability, security and performance are product requirements.
- Do not use mock data as real production data.
- Do not silently replace unavailable backend functionality with local-only functionality.
- Clearly distinguish sample previews, test fixtures and actual user records.
- All critical business rules must be enforced on the server.
- Do not claim compliance or certification without appropriate verification.

0.2 Product success philosophy

The objective is not to maximize:

- Time spent unnecessarily.
- Number of AI conversations.
- Vocabulary cards opened.
- Daily meaningless page visits.
- Artificial engagement.
- Unverified XP or streaks.

The objective is to improve:

- Communication ability.
- Language comprehension.
- Sentence construction.
- Speaking performance.
- Knowledge retention.
- Real-world task completion.
- Contextual language use.
- Learner confidence, measured separately as self-reported and behaviorally observed information.

0.3 Product truth policy

Every feature must have a defined implementation status:

- NOT STARTED
- IN PROGRESS
- IMPLEMENTED
- TESTED
- VERIFIED IN RUNTIME
- PRODUCTION VERIFIED
- BLOCKED
- DEFERRED

These statuses must never be treated as interchangeable.

A button existing in the frontend does not prove that its feature works.

An API returning HTTP 200 does not prove that its business operation is correct.

A successful build does not prove that the application works correctly at runtime.

A deployment command succeeding does not prove that the production application is healthy.

