4. COMMUNICATION IMPROVEMENT LOOP

This is the most important system in LINGUAVERSE AI.

4.1 Workflow

STEP 1 — DETECT

Identify actual weaknesses from exercises, conversations and assessments.

STEP 2 — EXPLAIN

Explain the mistake in language appropriate to the learner.

STEP 3 — PERSONALIZE

Create exercises targeting the identified weakness.

STEP 4 — PRACTICE

Let the learner apply the correction.

STEP 5 — TRANSFER

Test the concept in a different communication context.

STEP 6 — RETEST

Measure whether performance improved.

STEP 7 — UPDATE

Update the learner profile using verified evidence.

STEP 8 — REPEAT

Generate the next appropriate learning recommendation.

4.2 Evidence requirements

Every learning recommendation must contain:

- Recommendation reason.
- Supporting assessment or mistake references.
- Difficulty.
- Learning objective.
- Expected activity.
- Completion criteria.
- Recommendation timestamp.
- Recommendation algorithm version.

4.3 Success measurement

Measure:

- Mistake recurrence rate.
- Correct application rate.
- Retention after a time interval.
- Scenario completion.
- Assessment improvement.
- Transfer performance.
- Independent task performance.

Do not interpret correlation as proof that one specific lesson caused an improvement.

