9.5 Pronunciation assessment

Do not use ordinary speech recognition as proof of pronunciation correctness.

Where supported, use:

- Phoneme-level assessment.
- Forced alignment.
- Word-level pronunciation evidence.
- Supported acoustic indicators.
- Reference audio comparison.

Separate:

- Recognition accuracy.
- Pronunciation quality.
- Fluency.
- Grammar.
- Communication effectiveness.

Do not penalize legitimate accent variation.

Do not claim native-like pronunciation is required.

9.6 Real-time voice

Real-time voice is optional and must be implemented only when the selected provider and architecture genuinely support streaming.

Requirements:

- Streaming session management.
- Connection recovery.
- Audio buffering.
- Interruption handling.
- Latency measurement.
- Usage accounting.
- Graceful fallback.

A normal recorded-audio workflow must not be presented as real-time conversation.

9.7 Failure handling

