10. AI INTELLIGENCE AND EVALUATION FRAMEWORK

10.1 Provider abstraction

Implement provider-independent interfaces for:

- Language models.
- Speech recognition.
- Text-to-speech.
- Pronunciation assessment.

Do not couple application business logic directly to one vendor.

10.2 Provider selection

Select providers based on:

- Language support.
- Accent coverage.
- Latency.
- Cost.
- Reliability.
- Data processing terms.
- Privacy requirements.
- Availability.
- Quality benchmark results.

Keep provider configuration server-side.

10.3 Structured AI responses

Require validated structured outputs.

Illustrative logical response:

{
  "assessment_status": "completed",
  "transcript": "I went to school yesterday.",
  "feedback": [
    {
      "category": "grammar",
      "original": "I go to school yesterday.",
      "corrected": "I went to school yesterday.",
      "explanation": "Use past tense for a completed past event.",
      "confidence": 0.96
    }
  ],
  "recommendations": [
    "Practice past-tense sentence construction."
  ]
}

This is an illustrative schema, not actual assessment output.

Validate every field server-side.

Reject malformed, unsupported or incomplete outputs.

10.4 Prompt management

Implement:

- Versioned prompts.
- Prompt ownership.
- Change history.
- Evaluation datasets.
- Rollback capability.
- Provider/model version tracking.
- Prompt injection tests.

10.5 AI evaluation dataset

Maintain appropriately licensed or consented test examples.

Include:

- Beginner English.
- Intermediate English.
- Advanced English.
- Bangla-influenced English.
- Different legitimate accents.
- Noisy recordings.
- Ambiguous expressions.
- Grammar variations.
- Correct but uncommon expressions.
- Context-dependent expressions.

10.6 Evaluation metrics

Track:

- Correction precision.
- False correction rate.
- Explanation quality.
- Contextual relevance.
- Pronunciation reliability.
- Transcript error rate.
- Safety.
- Consistency.
- Latency.
- Cost per completed session.

Use human-reviewed ground truth for important evaluations.

An LLM's own confidence score is not proof of accuracy.

10.7 Human review

Provide review workflows for:

- Reported incorrect corrections.
- Systematic evaluation errors.
- Curriculum issues.
- Safety incidents.

Do not require manual review for every ordinary practice session.

