40. DEPLOYMENT AND ENVIRONMENT MANAGEMENT

40.1 Environments

Separate:

- Local development.
- Testing.
- Staging.
- Production.

Do not use production secrets in local test files.

40.2 Deployment

Use reproducible build and deployment workflows.

Verify:

- Build.
- Environment configuration.
- Database migrations.
- Worker bindings.
- R2 access.
- Queue configuration.
- Cron configuration.
- Turnstile configuration.
- Custom domain.
- HTTPS.
- Production health endpoint.

40.3 Secret management

- Store provider credentials using secure server-side secret configuration.
- Never hardcode secrets.
- Never commit secrets.
- Never print secrets in logs.
- Use least-privilege tokens.
- Rotate compromised credentials.
- Do not request users to paste production API tokens into chat.

40.4 Production verification

After deployment, verify:

- Live URL responds.
- Health endpoint responds.
- Frontend loads.
- Authentication works.
- Backend routes work.
- Database connectivity works.
- Critical user workflows work.
- No critical console errors.
- No critical server errors.

A deployment command alone is not production verification.

